From: MrLGamer <mrlgam3r@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:08:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: winex11: let the Kuro launcher's WebView2 ignore noopwr

Proton turns off other-process rendering for Wuthering Waves (noopwr).
The Steam build starts the Kuro launcher under the same app id, and its
bundled WebView2 runtime renders its page from another process, so the
launcher page stays blank under that setting. Let that runtime ignore it.

Only applies to the launcher's KRWebViewRuntime.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/init.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
@@ -1002,7 +1002,8 @@
     if (disable == -1)
     {
         const char *e = getenv( "WINE_DISABLE_VULKAN_OPWR" );
-        disable = e && atoi( e );
+        /* the launcher's WebView2 needs OPWR, even under Proton's noopwr for the game */
+        disable = e && atoi( e ) && !is_kuro_webview_process();
     }
     return disable;
 }
